  mask:
    color: 5 (always the unique largest non-bg color)
    bbox: 5-10 rows x 5-10 cols (the output region)
    single 4-connected component
    density: 0.60-0.71 of bbox (rest are bg holes)
    every row and column of bbox contains >=1 mask pixel
  palette:
    shape: 3 rows x W cols where W = mask bbox width
    row 0 and row 1 identical (column-color pattern of 4-5 contiguous runs, run length 1-3)
    row 2 uniform single hole_color
    3-5 distinct column colors, all different from bg, mask_color, and hole_color
    hole_color also different from bg and mask_color
  layout:
    mask and palette occupy disjoint row bands, gap 1-3 empty rows
    either can be above or below the other [observed]
    column ranges may differ (not aligned) but both fit within grid
  output:
    crop to mask bbox; mask pixels get column color from palette row 0; bg holes get hole_color

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size H x W (10-18 each), mask bbox size mh x mw (5-10 each).
    2. Choose 3-5 distinct column colors + 1 hole_color + mask_color=5, all mutually distinct and != 0.
    3. Build palette row as contiguous color runs totalling mw columns (4-5 runs, lengths 1-3).
